A minor success report:  The re(4) driver works on 5.1-CURRENT/alpha
on PC164 for a RealTek 8169S-based GigE card.

re0: <RealTek 8110S Single-chip Gigabit Ethernet> port 0x10200-0x102ff mem 0x82835200-0x828352ff irq 2 at device 5.0 on pci0
re0: Ethernet address: 00:08:54:d0:33:44
miibus0: <MII bus> on re0
rgephy0: <RTL8169S/8110S media interface> on miibus0
rgephy0:  10baseT, 10baseT-FDX, 100baseTX, 100baseTX-FDX, 1000baseTX, 1000baseTX-FDX, auto
re0: interrupting at CIA irq 2

$ ifconfig re0 | grep media
	media: Ethernet autoselect (1000baseTX <full-duplex>)

(It's an OEM card sold in Germany by Starchip as "SGE-9230TX-32"
individually or as part of their switch + 2 NICs bundle.)

